    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 8,
    "title": "Express some and each",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-quantity-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Express some and each",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "一些 gives an unspecified amount. In a statement, 几 can give a small unspecified number. 每 distributes a statement over individual members, with a suitable classifier; ordinary nouns do not need a plural ending.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "我有一些书。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yǒu yīxiē shū 。",
                "meaning": "I have some books.",
                "audio": "06824c46cb264ab0c6f7b69663dd1ce536743b1d0e0e8255e68eafb8ee852b18"
              },
              {
                "text": "我有几本书。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yǒu jǐ běn shū 。",
                "meaning": "I have a few books.",
                "audio": "029b282396b8b7bfb78a22bfff888d88c634e725c808c9db5edcfb51e2464436"
              },
              {
                "text": "每个人都有书。",
                "pinyin": "měi gè rén dōu yǒu shū 。",
                "meaning": "Every person has a book.",
                "audio": "9fed18f83257bc4b41f79ea51c95221723e7e7ab67e75f8ae5e5195cff190311"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
